{% doc %}
  Header — ARCHITECTURE.md §6.2 · T-051, T-008, T-045 (text-roll).

  Re-skinned (Sep 2026, owner's direction): every page now wears the
  homepage's pill nav — the emblem standing alone, the link capsule, the
  Catalogue pill and the search/cart roundels — so the chrome is ONE design
  on both grounds. Values are copied from sv-hero-video's pill nav; only
  the pills wear the brand emerald here (owner's direction, Sep 2026)
  rather than the hero's dark film glass.

  Scroll state still comes from an IntersectionObserver on a zero-height
  sentinel via sv-motion.js ([data-header]/[data-header-sentinel]); the
  pills carry their own ground, so the header bar itself stays transparent
  in both states. No scroll listeners anywhere.

  Navigation renders whatever menu Shopify holds. Menus are business data
  and belong to the store owner.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign menu = linklists[section.settings.menu]
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The skip link is rendered in layout/theme.liquid, not here — it must be the
  first focusable element in the document.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Site typography — ONE pair on every page (owner's direction, 22 Sep
  2026): Georgia for headings, prices and display text; the device's
  own system font for everything else (San Francisco on Apple, Segoe UI
  on Windows, Roboto on Android). Tried and rejected the same day: Jost +
  EB Garamond, then Inter. Set here because this header renders first on
  every template.

  · --serif: Georgia (Mac, iOS, Windows). Android has no Georgia, so
    Gelasio — a metric-compatible Georgia design, OFL, one variable woff2
    in assets — sits behind it and downloads only where Georgia is missing.
  · --sans and Horizon's body/subheading/accent variables all point at
    the system stack, so collection, search and blog pages match the
    rebuilt ones. No text font is downloaded at all.
  · sv-system.css still names Jost/EB Garamond; these :root values
    override it because this rule comes later in the document.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Gelasio';
    src: url("{{ 'sv-gelasio.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Gelasio';
    src: url("{{ 'sv-gelasio-italic.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  :root {
    --sv-system: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    --sv-georgia: Georgia, 'Gelasio', 'Times New Roman', serif;
    --sans: var(--sv-system);
    --serif: var(--sv-georgia);
    --font-body--family: var(--sv-system);
    --font-subheading--family: var(--sv-system);
    --font-accent--family: var(--sv-system);
    --font-heading--family: var(--sv-georgia);
  }
  /* Browsers give form controls their own font (Arial); zero specificity,
     so any control that names a font still wins. */
  :where(button, input, select, textarea) {
    font-family: inherit;
  }
</style>

<div data-header-sentinel aria-hidden="true"></div>

<header class="sv-header" data-header data-sv>
  <div class="sv-header__inner w w--wide">
    {%- comment -%}
      The mark stands alone — no pill, no ground (hero rule). Below 64px
      the 24-petal emblem blurs; the 8-path simple variant is the same
      mark drawn for small sizes (brand system §2).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a class="sv-header__mark" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
      <img src="{{ 'emblem-colour.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="68" height="68">
    </a>

    {%- if menu.links.size > 0 -%}
      <nav class="sv-header__pill" aria-label="{{ menu.title | escape }}">
        {%- for link in menu.links -%}
          <div class="sv-header__item">
            {%- comment -%}
              aria-label repeats the visible label exactly (WCAG 2.5.3); the
              text-roll splits it across two spans and the duplicated span
              carries aria-hidden.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <a class="sv-header__link" href="{{ link.url }}" aria-label="{{ link.title | escape }}" {% if link.current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
              <span class="roll">
                <span>{{ link.title }}</span>
                <span aria-hidden="true">{{ link.title }}</span>
              </span>
            </a>

            {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Shop by Age carries a third level, and stacking every size
                under every age made a panel taller than the window. The
                ages become a column and the sizes fly out beside the one
                being read — one age's run at a time, the whole list never
                more than a glance deep. A menu without a third level is
                untouched and stays the plain column it always was.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign split = false
                for child in link.links
                  if child.links.size > 0
                    assign split = true
                    break
                  endif
                endfor
              -%}
              <ul class="sv-header__sub{% if split %} sv-header__sub--split{% endif %}">
                {%- for child in link.links -%}
                  <li class="sv-header__group{% if forloop.first %} is-first{% endif %}">
                    <a class="sv-header__sub-link" href="{{ child.url }}">
                      {{ child.title }}
                      {%- if child.links.size > 0 -%}
                        <svg class="sv-header__caret" viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4.5 2.5L8 6l-3.5 3.5"/></svg>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                    {%- if child.links.size > 0 -%}
                      <div class="sv-header__flyout">
                        <p class="sv-header__flyout-head">{{ child.title }}</p>
                        <ul class="sv-header__chips" aria-label="{{ child.title | escape }}">
                          {%- for grandchild in child.links -%}
                            <li><a class="sv-header__chip" href="{{ grandchild.url }}">{{ grandchild.title }}</a></li>
                          {%- endfor -%}
                        </ul>
                      </div>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="sv-header__side">
      {%- comment -%}
        Mobile navigation. <details> is a native disclosure: keyboard
        operable, announced by screen readers, no JavaScript.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <details class="sv-header__drawer">
        <summary class="sv-header__roundbtn" aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.menu' | t | default: 'Menu' }}">
          {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'menu', class: 'sv-header__glyph sv-header__glyph--open' %}
          {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'close', class: 'sv-header__glyph sv-header__glyph--close' %}
        </summary>

        <nav class="sv-header__sheet" aria-label="{{ menu.title | escape }}">
          <ul class="sv-header__sheet-list">
            {%- for link in menu.links -%}
              <li>
                <a class="act sv-header__sheet-link" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a>
                {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
                  <ul class="sv-header__sheet-sub">
                    {%- for child in link.links -%}
                      <li>
                        <a class="sv-header__sheet-child" href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title }}</a>
                        {%- if child.links.size > 0 -%}
                          <ul class="sv-header__chips sv-header__chips--sheet" aria-label="{{ child.title | escape }}">
                            {%- for grandchild in child.links -%}
                              <li><a class="sv-header__chip" href="{{ grandchild.url }}">{{ grandchild.title }}</a></li>
                            {%- endfor -%}
                          </ul>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </li>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </ul>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The sheet is the phone's full navigation, so the account
              entry lives here too — the label says which door it is.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <li>
              <a class="act sv-header__sheet-link" href="{{ routes.root_url | append: 'pages/wishlist' | replace: '//', '/' }}">Wishlist</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a class="act sv-header__sheet-link" href="{% if customer %}{{ routes.account_url }}{% else %}{{ routes.account_login_url }}{% endif %}">
                {%- if customer -%}
                  {{ 'accessibility.account' | t | default: 'Account' }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ 'actions.log_in' | t | default: 'Sign in' }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </details>

      {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
        <a class="sv-header__cta" href="{{ section.settings.cta_url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ section.settings.cta_label }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}

      <a class="sv-header__roundbtn" href="{{ routes.search_url }}" aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.search' | t | default: 'Search' }}">
        {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'search' %}
      </a>

      {%- comment -%}
        Account entry (new customer accounts: routes.account_url and
        routes.account_login_url both land on the hosted passwordless
        pages at account.sahasravastra.com). Desktop only — on phones the
        bottom bar already owns Account, and a fourth roundel would crowd
        the row.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a class="sv-header__roundbtn sv-header__roundbtn--account" href="{% if customer %}{{ routes.account_url }}{% else %}{{ routes.account_login_url }}{% endif %}" aria-label="{% if customer %}{{ 'accessibility.account' | t | default: 'Account' }}{% else %}{{ 'actions.log_in' | t | default: 'Sign in' }}{% endif %}">
        {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'account' %}
      </a>

      {%- comment -%} Wishlist, beside the cart. Desktop, like Account — phones reach it from the menu sheet. {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'sv-saved-link', class: 'sv-header__roundbtn sv-header__roundbtn--account' %}

      <a class="sv-header__roundbtn" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.cart_count' | t: count: cart.item_count }}">
        {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'cart' %}
        {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
          <span class="sv-header__count" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<script>
  (() => {
    const header = document.querySelector('.sv-header');
    const side = header && header.querySelector('.sv-header__side');
    const inner = header && header.querySelector('.sv-header__inner');
    if (!side || !inner || !('ResizeObserver' in window)) return;
    const set = () => {
      header.style.setProperty('--sv-side-reserve', '0px');
      if (!window.matchMedia('(min-width: 1080px)').matches) return;
      /* With the reserve at 0 the padding is .w's gutter; how far does the
         cluster reach into the column from there? */
      const box = inner.getBoundingClientRect();
      const reach = box.right - (side.getBoundingClientRect().left - 16);
      if (reach > 0) header.style.setProperty('--sv-side-reserve', reach + 'px');
    };
    const ro = new ResizeObserver(set);
    ro.observe(side);
    ro.observe(document.documentElement);
    set();
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Colour and spacing are tokens only. The pill values mirror
     sv-hero-video's nav: Jost 600 / 0.76rem / 0.14em, 999px capsules,
     54px roundels — one chrome, both grounds. */

  /* The whole header group sticks (announcement + pills), matching the
     homepage's fixed chrome. Sticky sits on the GROUP: the header alone is
     trapped inside #header-group's own height and would scroll away. On
     the homepage the group is empty (the hero hides both members), so the
     sticky wrapper is inert there. */
  #header-group {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 60;
  }

  /* A standing cream wash — over the page top it vanishes into the ivory
     ground, over scrolled content it keeps text from threading between
     the pills. Unconditional: the scroll sentinel sticks with the group,
     so a toggled state could never fire. No backdrop-filter here — a
     filter would make the header the containing block for the drawer's
     position:fixed sheet. */
  [data-sv].sv-header {
    background: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.96);
    padding: var(--a) 0;
  }

  .sv-header__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--a);
  }

  .sv-header__mark {
    display: block;
    justify-self: start;
  }

  .sv-header__mark img {
    /* Matches the capsule's height, per the owner. Horizon's global
       max-width cap resolves circularly in the shrink-to-fit grid cell
       and collapsed the mark — released explicitly. */
    width: 68px;
    height: 68px;
    max-width: none;
    display: block;
    transition: transform 0.7s var(--e);
  }

  .sv-header__mark:hover img {
    transform: rotate(120deg) scale(1.06);
  }

  /* The capsule, in the brand emerald. */
  .sv-header__pill {
    display: none;
    justify-self: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 7px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--emerald);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.22);
  }

  .sv-header__item {
    position: relative;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__link {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    /* Matches the hero nav, which is set to the hero cards' text size. */
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--cream);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 15px 24px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__link:hover,
  [data-sv] .sv-header__link:focus-visible {
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__link:hover .roll > span,
  [data-sv] .sv-header__link:focus-visible .roll > span {
    transform: translateY(-1.15em);
  }

  /* Dropdown: the hero's dark panel. Disclosure, not animation —
     focus-within keeps it keyboard reachable. */
  .sv-header__sub {
    display: none;
    position: absolute;
    top: 100%;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 70;
    min-width: max-content;
    padding: 10px;
    margin-top: 8px;
    border-radius: 22px;
    background: var(--emerald);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.22);
  }

  .sv-header__item:hover .sv-header__sub,
  .sv-header__item:focus-within .sv-header__sub {
    display: block;
  }

  .sv-header__sub-link {
    display: block;
    padding: 11px 18px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--cream);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .sv-header__sub-link:hover,
  .sv-header__sub-link:focus-visible {
    background: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.16);
  }

  /* Two panes: ages down the left, the read age's sizes beside them.
     The flyout is a sibling of the age link, positioned out of the
     column, so nothing in the left list moves as it opens. */
  .sv-header__sub--split {
    padding-right: 10px;
  }

  .sv-header__group {
    position: relative;
  }

  .sv-header__sub-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .sv-header__caret {
    inline-size: 12px;
    block-size: 12px;
    opacity: 0.6;
    flex: none;
  }

  .sv-header__flyout {
    display: none;
    position: absolute;
    top: -10px;
    left: 100%;
    margin-left: 10px;
    z-index: 71;
    width: max-content;
    /* Wide enough for a whole age's run on one line — three sizes for
       Toddler, four for Newborn — so a panel never breaks a set across
       two rows and reads as two groups. */
    max-width: 480px;
    padding: 14px 16px 16px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: var(--emerald);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.22);
  }

  /* Hover or keyboard focus opens an age; with neither, the first age is
     already open so the panel never reads as half-built. */
  .sv-header__group:hover > .sv-header__flyout,
  .sv-header__group:focus-within > .sv-header__flyout,
  .sv-header__sub--split:not(:hover):not(:focus-within) .sv-header__group.is-first > .sv-header__flyout {
    display: block;
  }

  .sv-header__group:hover > .sv-header__sub-link,
  .sv-header__group:focus-within > .sv-header__sub-link,
  .sv-header__sub--split:not(:hover):not(:focus-within) .sv-header__group.is-first > .sv-header__sub-link {
    background: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.16);
  }

  .sv-header__flyout-head {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.62);
  }

  /* Third level: size chips under their age row. The panel is sized by
     its widest row, so chips wrap inside a capped width rather than
     stretching it. */
  /* [data-sv] lifts these past sv-system's §02 list reset (0,1,1). */
  [data-sv] .sv-header__chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    max-width: 280px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 18px 12px;
    list-style: none;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__chip {
    display: block;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.4);
    color: var(--cream);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__chip:hover,
  [data-sv] .sv-header__chip:focus-visible {
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* On the cream sheet the chips take ink. */
  [data-sv] .sv-header__chips--sheet {
    max-width: none;
    padding: 0 0 var(--a);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__chips--sheet .sv-header__chip {
    border-color: var(--line, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.2));
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__chips--sheet .sv-header__chip:hover {
    background: var(--emerald);
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  /* The right cluster: Catalogue pill and the roundels. On desktop it
     leaves the .w grid and anchors to the bar's own corner (owner's
     call, Sep 2026): the roundels hug the top-right of the SCREEN, not
     the content column, and the social float below matches — 14px here
     + 54px roundel and 16px + 50px mark share one centre line. */
  .sv-header__side {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--a);
    justify-self: end;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1080px) {
    [data-sv].sv-header {
      position: relative;
    }
    .sv-header__side {
      position: absolute;
      right: 14px;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
    }
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__cta {
    display: none;
    align-items: center;
    height: 54px;
    padding-inline: 28px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--emerald);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.22);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cream);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-header__cta:hover {
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-header__roundbtn {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 54px;
    height: 54px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--emerald);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.22);
    color: var(--cream);
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    position: relative;
    transition: background 0.3s ease;
  }

  .sv-header__roundbtn:hover {
    background: var(--emerald-d);
  }

  /* Phones reach the account through the bottom bar and the menu sheet. */
  .sv-header__roundbtn--account {
    display: none;
  }

  .sv-header__roundbtn svg {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
  }

  .sv-header__count {
    position: absolute;
    top: -2px;
    right: -2px;
    min-width: var(--a);
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--tan);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    line-height: var(--a);
  }

  /* ── mobile drawer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-header__drawer > summary {
    list-style: none;
  }

  .sv-header__drawer > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .sv-header__drawer:not([open]) .sv-header__glyph--close,
  .sv-header__drawer[open] .sv-header__glyph--open {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The open sheet is fixed at z-index 80; the summary must ride above it
     or the close button paints underneath its own overlay. */
  .sv-header__drawer[open] > summary {
    z-index: 90;
  }

  .sv-header__sheet {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 80;
    background: var(--cream);
    padding: var(--f) var(--b) var(--d);
    overflow-y: auto;
  }

  .sv-header__sheet-list > li + li {
    margin-top: var(--b);
  }

  .sv-header__sheet-link {
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .sv-header__sheet-sub {
    margin-top: var(--a);
  }

  .sv-header__sheet-child {
    display: block;
    padding: var(--a) 0;
    color: var(--grey);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
  }

  .sv-header__sheet-child:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* ── desktop ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (min-width: 1080px) {
    .sv-header__drawer {
      display: none;
    }

    .sv-header__pill {
      display: flex;
    }

    [data-sv] .sv-header__cta {
      display: flex;
    }

    .sv-header__roundbtn--account {
      display: flex;
    }
  }

  /* Narrow desktop: the full row does not fit beside the emblem, so the
     labels tighten and the Catalogue pill steps out. Upper bound sized
     to the full row's own width — raised to 1480 when Saved joined the
     cluster, measured so the pill never meets the roundels. */
  /* The right cluster is absolutely placed (it hugs the screen corner),
     so nothing stops the centred pill from sliding under it. Reserve its
     width on the inner grid instead — only as much as the cluster
     actually intrudes into the .w column, measured by the script below
     as --sv-side-reserve (0 on wide screens) — so the pill never
     overlaps, however many roundels the cluster holds
     (Saved joined it in Sep 2026 and caused a 147px overlap at 1280). */
  @media (min-width: 1080px) {
    /* Never less than .w's own gutter (--c at this width). */
    .sv-header__inner {
      padding-right: max(var(--c), var(--sv-side-reserve, 0px));
    }
  }

  /* Desktop layout starts at 1080, not 880 (Sep 2026): measured, the full
     link row + emblem + roundel cluster needs ~1080px even compacted —
     at 900 the pill ran 163px under the roundels. 880–1079 now wears
     the menu-sheet layout. */
  @media (min-width: 1080px) and (max-width: 1480px) {
    [data-sv] .sv-header__link {
      padding: 13px 13px;
      /* Steps down from the 0.85rem base, in step with the hero nav. */
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    }

    [data-sv] .sv-header__cta {
      display: none;
    }

    .sv-header__roundbtn {
      width: 46px;
      height: 46px;
    }

    .sv-header__mark img {
      width: 54px;
      height: 54px;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Header",
  "tag": "section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": [
      "header"
    ]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "menu",
      "label": "Menu",
      "default": "main-menu",
      "info": "Edit the menu itself in Content → Menus. The theme renders whatever it holds."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Pill button label",
      "default": "Catalogue"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_url",
      "label": "Pill button link",
      "info": "Defaults to the all-products catalogue when left empty."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
